#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Navigation.rst:2
msgid "Navigation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Navigation.rst:10
msgid ""
"Navigation capabilities enable a robot to map its position in an environment "
"and plan the path to a new destination. This article summarizes ROS "
"developer tools and guidance available to help with navigation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Navigation.rst:13
msgid ""
"**Area: navigation, capabilities | Content-type: about | Experience: "
"beginner, intermediate, expert**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Navigation.rst:16
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Navigation.rst:19
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Navigation.rst:21
msgid ""
"Navigation capabilities enable a mobile robot to map its environment, plan a "
"path to a new destination, and then control movement along that path "
"including handling unexpected interruptions, such as an unforeseen obstacle, "
"that happen as it moves."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Navigation.rst:23
msgid ""
"ROS also includes motion planning capabilities. See :doc:`About-Motion-"
"planning`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Navigation.rst:26
msgid "ROS capabilities are enabled by community-contributed packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Navigation.rst:29
msgid "Community-contributed packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Navigation.rst:31
msgid ""
"`Nav2 <https://nav2.org/>`_: An industry-standard mobile robot navigation "
"system for mobile and surface robotics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Navigation.rst:33
msgid ""
"`EasyNav <https://github.com/EasyNavigation/>`_: A flexible, extensible "
"navigation system for mobile robots."
msgstr ""
